# The free Quake II data the CI runs its server-driven checks on, member by
# member, in the layout `q2data.sh` writes it to.  id's two freely downloadable
# archives are the source: the 3.20 point release with CTF
# (`q2-3.20-x86-full-ctf.exe`) and the 3.14 demo (`q2-314-demo-x86.exe`).
#
# The paks are the ones yquake2's installation notes publish MD5s for
# (`doc/020_installation.md`), and they were checked against those before these
# SHA-256s were recorded -- 2026-09-23, from deponie.yamagi.org, whose Wayback
# copy was byte-identical on the same day.  The two licence texts ride along
# because the demo's grant of free electronic distribution holds "so long as
# this Agreement accompanies the Software at all times", and a tree that is
# only ever used, never shipped, might as well carry its terms too.
